Ghostlane's one change to sing-box v1.13.14 (patch -p1 in the module's tree;
scripts/patched-singbox.sh applies it for every build: the CLI, Android, the
desktops and the iOS Cores).

A Reality line opens on current Xray servers.

1. The hello keeps its X25519MLKEM768 key share. sing-box strips it from every
   Reality hello (since its commit dbdcce20a8, 2025, no option, no reason
   given; upstream `testing` still does on 2026-11-11). XTLS/REALITY 8cdf7bf
   (2026-09-08, in Xray-core from v26.9.8) forwards a hello without one ahead
   of X25519 to the camouflage target, so the line never opens. Xray-core's
   own client never strips it.
2. A fingerprint whose hello has no such share in this uTLS (firefox, safari,
   ios, edge, 360, qq, android; `random` four times in five) is sent as
   Chrome's, the only hello here that has it.
3. The hello announces 26.7.11 instead of 1.8.1. Xray-core v26.7.x servers
   with no minClientVer configured refuse anything below 26.3.27.

Measured on 2026-11-11 against the official Xray-linux-64 builds, VLESS +
Reality + Vision: unpatched, the chrome hello opens on v26.4.25 only and is
refused by v26.7.11 and v26.11.9; patched, chrome, firefox, safari, ios,
random and randomized open on all three.

